# Starforge Universe site concept

Preserve this product and design concept in all UI, copy, and frontend changes.

## Brand and storytelling

- Brand name: **Starforge Universe** (hero-level, not only nav text).
- Tone: Apple-style scroll storytelling — sparse sections, one job per section, large expressive type.
- Hybrid visual system: cinematic **deep-space hero** + quieter **light paper stage** content sections.
- Support **dark and light** themes (`data-theme` on `html`, `ThemeService`, persisted). Both modes must remain viable.
- Fonts: Syne (display) + Manrope (body). Do not switch to Inter/Roboto/Arial/system stacks.
- Accents: cool starlight / teal-metal — not purple glow defaults. On light stages, use dark stage eyebrow tokens (`--sf-stage-eyebrow`) for contrast.
- Motion: ambient stars/parallax, scroll reveals, route view transitions. Prefer `opacity`/`transform`; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Navigation (no page-load feel)

- Keep app shell (ambient background + sticky nav) mounted across routes.
- Home: `''`. Product detail: `/lines/:slug`. Unknown slug: in-page missing state; unknown path: 404.
- Use `routerLink` / `Router` + `withViewTransitions()` — never full document reloads for product selection.
- Detail views always offer a clear **Back to universe** path.
- Sticky nav uses an Apple-style full-width hover mega pane. Menu entries come from catalog nested `products`, or **Coming soon** when a line has none yet. Do not hard-code mega-menu rows in the template.

## Product lines (extendable)

- Single source of truth: [`src/app/data/product-lines.ts`](src/app/data/product-lines.ts).
- To add a product line, **only add a catalog entry** (slug, name, tagline, summary, status, story blocks). Home list and nav must stay data-driven — do not hard-code product rows in templates.
- Category lines (for example Utilities) may include nested `products`. Add tools there to extend the category without new hard-coded UI.
- Current lines:
  - `project-templating` — Starforge project templating (available): GitHub templates, CI/CD, layout, conventions.
  - `all-seeing-eye` — All Seeing Eye (building): discoverability and monitoring of codebase state across a project universe; dependencies/integrations for compliance; architectural overview of GitHub repos. Frame as in progress / growing — do not oversell.
  - `utilities` — Utilities (available): category of developer productivity tools. Nested `products` grow this line; first tool is LiquiSketch (Liquibase changelogs → Draw.io schema diagrams). Add more utilities via `products`, not hard-coded templates.

## Home section order

1. Hero — brand, one headline, one lead, one CTA group; no product grid in the first viewport.
2. Introduction — what Starforge Universe is.
3. Product lines — catalog-driven list linking to details.
4. Closing — quiet invitation; universe still expanding.

## Do not

- Replace the hybrid cosmic/stage system with a generic dashboard or purple-gradient AI look.
- Put cards, badges, or promo chips on top of hero media.
- Duplicate product copy outside the catalog when the catalog already owns it.
